        "publishedAt": "2026-03-16T22:05:22.597471+00:00",
        "description": "<p>A 3D-modeling project inspired by the <a href=\"https://theme.npm.edu.tw/exh106/npm_anime/cabbage/en/index.html\">Jadeite Cabbage</a> in the Taiwan National Palace Museum.</p>\n<p>Tools used are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ZBrush</strong> for sculpting:<ul>\n<li>an initial dynamics simulation of leaves folded around the hull shape</li>\n<li>refinement via curve tube brushes for natural vegetation stemming patterns</li>\n<li>details and leaf refinement via transpose and cloth simulation brushes</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Substance3D Painter</strong> for texture baking and overall material creation via layered detail buildup<ul>\n<li>Uses normal and height maps for structure enhancement</li>\n<li>Uses thickness map for Subsurface Scattering (SSS) appearance</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Maya Arnold</strong> for final rendering</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>To-Do:</strong> Increase likeness to the Jadeite Cabbage. Namely, the original model features a Locust Bug -- also sculpted in jade -- in the leaves, and a holding stand. The former being a priority.</p>",
